# Allowlist approach: ignore everything by default, then explicitly
# un-ignore only the active Jarvis system's own files. Far more robust
# than trying to enumerate this folder's many old backup folders
# individually (tried that first -- missed several; this folder has
# accumulated ~15+ old version snapshots from before git existed here).
# Nothing on disk is touched or deleted by any of this -- it only
# controls what git tracks going forward.
*

!.gitignore
!Jarvis_FINAL_WORKING.py
!Jarvis_Desktop_HUD.py
!jarvis_hud.html
!jarvis_memory.json
!START_JARVIS_FINAL_WORKING.bat
!eva_prompter.py
!host_agent_processor.py
!jarvis_ask_user_mcp.py
!jarvis_launcher.py
!_active_dev_session.json

# LibreHardwareMonitor: vendored third-party tool, not source code --
# only track our own config for it, not its ~19MB of binaries/DLLs.
!LibreHardwareMonitor/
LibreHardwareMonitor/*
!LibreHardwareMonitor/LibreHardwareMonitor.config
